    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can confirm the correct property from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to help responders locate the turn-in during nighttime or low-visibility conditions.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles so emergency apparatus can reach both structures without obstruction.\n• Maintain adequate width and overhead clearance along the access drive to allow a fire engine or ambulance to reach the detached structure.\n• Post a simple site map near the driveway entrance showing the location of both structures, the parking area, and any utility shutoffs.\n• Designate a specific area away from the driveway for visitor parking so the access drive remains open for emergency vehicles.\n• Keep a gate or secondary path accessible at the far end of the driveway so vehicles can turn around without backing the full length of the drive.\n• Identify and mark a secondary exit route across open terrain in case the single driveway becomes blocked during an emergency.\n• Clearly number or label both the main residence and the detached structure so responders can immediately distinguish between them on arrival.\n• Keep the area between the two structures open and passable so responders can move freely between them on foot or with equipment."
  },
