    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing close to the structure on all sides.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to increase open space between the canopy and the building.\n• Mow or cut ground vegetation around the structure and along the driveway.\n• Remove shrubs growing along the driveway edge that could block vehicle movement or spread fire toward the access route.\n• Keep the single driveway clear of overhanging branches and low-growing shrubs along its full length.\n• Maintain open gaps between shrub clusters so fire cannot travel continuously from one to the next toward the structure.\n• Cut back ground vegetation in open terrain areas that connect directly to the structure."
